Forwarding Stripe's latest public announcement, summarized for diligence.

Stripe has signed agreements with investors to provide liquidity to current and former employees through a tender offer at a $159B valuation (February 24, 2026).
The majority of funds for the tender offer are provided by investors including Thrive Capital, Coatue, and a16z; Stripe will also use a portion of its own capital to repurchase shares.
Businesses running on Stripe generated $1.9 trillion in total volume in 2025, up 34% from 2024.
Stripe's Revenue suite is on track to hit an annual run rate of $1 billion this year.
Stripe powers more than 5 million businesses directly or via platforms, including 90% of the Dow Jones Industrial Average and 80% of the Nasdaq 100.
Stripe remained robustly profitable in 2025.
Patrick Collison is Cofounder and CEO. John Collison is Cofounder and President. Steffan Tomlinson is Chief Financial Officer.
Stripe has dual headquarters in San Francisco and Dublin.

